From: Connector2 firmware project
Subject: [PATCH] sandbox: recognize ARM EABI clock_gettime64 with old headers

The Bootlin toolchain has pre-time64 Linux headers but its glibc can invoke
clock_gettime64 on our Linux 6.12 kernel. The existing OpenSSH allow rule is
then omitted, killing the preauth child with SIGSYS (syscall 403). Supply
the ARM EABI number when missing; keep the existing seccomp policy intact.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [external toolchain header compatibility]

--- a/sandbox-seccomp-filter.c
+++ b/sandbox-seccomp-filter.c
@@ -58,6 +58,11 @@
 #include <elf.h>
 
 #include <asm/unistd.h>
+/* ARM EABI syscall table: clock_gettime64 = 403, added in Linux 5.1. */
+#if defined(__arm__) && defined(__ARM_EABI__) && !defined(__NR_clock_gettime64)
+# define __NR_clock_gettime64 403
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __s390__
 #include <asm/zcrypt.h>
 #endif
